WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.760
Devon now commits 89% of cognition's own code as the lab hits a $1 billion run rate. That figure sits on a $48 billion valuation. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 209. After cognition, we get X's Search API, Inception's diffusion model, the agent governance problem, and the local boxes people are actually wiring up. Then, things to try on the horizon and an engineering tear down. Cognition, ai magazine reports, posted the jump on

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:37.220
on September 25th, 2026, up from $492 million in May after raising more than $2 billion.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.920
Devon plans, writes, tests, and commits, and a human reviews what it produced.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:48.020
Scott Wu, the chief executive, says the agent currently lands between a junior and

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.160
a mid-level engineer.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:55.420
Goldman Sachs, Mercedes-Benz, GE Aerospace, and New Bank are on the customer list, with

00:00:55.420 --> 00:01:02.180
distribution deals at Infosys, Cognizant, and AWS. Mercedes-Benz put more than 200,000

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:07.460
lines of cobalt through Devon, and new banks saw 8-12 times efficiency gains on large

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:14.160
migrations. Cognition bought wind surf in July 2025 and gained an agentic integrated development

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.720
environment, or IDE, that sits beside Devon in a working developer's day.

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:25.620
Exis shipped Exis 3.0 as an upgrade to its web search API for AI agents.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:31.160
Mark Tech post reports, with a larger embedding model and a cheaper light search type priced

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:33.140
at $4 per 1000 requests.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:38.700
Dynamic highlights is now generally available and it picks tokens across results instead

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:39.760
of page by page.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:46.200
That path uses 95% fewer tokens than full page text and still improves answer quality.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:51.420
Excess says the new version leads perplexity, brave, and parallel on all eight of its

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:58.840
self-run benchmarks, with the widest gaps on browse comp at 91.8% and atlas at 42%.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:03.860
The company runs its own crawler and an independent index covering more than two trillion URLs,

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:06.180
and there is no self-hosted option.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:12.420
Light accepts query, result count, highlights, text, categories, domain and date filters,

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.380
plus location and moderation.

00:02:15.733 --> 00:02:18.993
Mercury III, a diffusion language model from Inception,

00:02:19.693 --> 00:02:22.593
fills in many tokens at once instead of one after another,

00:02:23.113 --> 00:02:24.213
Mark Tech Post reports.

00:02:24.873 --> 00:02:28.873
It hits 1068 tokens per second on Nvidia GPUs

00:02:28.873 --> 00:02:31.633
and carries a 1 million token context window.

00:02:32.213 --> 00:02:36.213
On Inception's own table, Mercury III leads GPT-6 Luna

00:02:36.213 --> 00:02:40.793
and Claude Haiku 5.5 on 8 of 12 tests at medium settings.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:44.593
with its biggest gains on instruction following and agentic coding.

00:02:44.893 --> 00:02:50.313
The model is more than 40 times larger than Mercury 1, and average quality across standard

00:02:50.313 --> 00:02:55.933
benchmarks rose roughly three times across those generations, while speed stayed above 1,000

00:02:55.933 --> 00:02:56.873
tokens per second.

00:02:57.493 --> 00:03:03.293
Serving is only through Inception's NVIDIA GPU API, with no open weights and no quantized

00:03:03.293 --> 00:03:03.673
builds.

00:03:05.376 --> 00:03:13.896
The author of Cynthia put out Tess 4.5 to 27b, a Quinn 3.8 to 27b fine-tune in the local

00:03:13.896 --> 00:03:15.336
Lama community on Reddit.

00:03:15.856 --> 00:03:20.076
It matches the same benchmark scores with 25% fewer tokens overall.

00:03:20.736 --> 00:03:27.296
On the hardest subsets, CLI 40 and data extraction, the cut is 32 to 43% fewer tokens.

00:03:28.216 --> 00:03:30.376
GGUF weights are up on hugging face.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:34.796
burning fewer tokens means faster answers and longer sessions before the

00:03:34.796 --> 00:03:41.222
context window fills, and that stacks with draft head acceleration on local GPUs.

00:03:41.682 --> 00:03:45.762
Enterprises now have to track and secure their own proliferating AI agents,

00:03:46.182 --> 00:03:51.642
not only fend off external rogue ones, CIO reports. Most organizations still lack

00:03:51.642 --> 00:03:56.862
basic visibility, and Thropic says 82% have found unregistered agents on their

00:03:56.862 --> 00:04:04.162
networks, and 57% already run agents on multi-stage workflows. Standing up an agent is one API call,

00:04:04.482 --> 00:04:10.622
or vibe coding by any employee, so vendor, platform native, and homegrown agents pile onto the sprawl.

00:04:11.102 --> 00:04:16.482
Security teams need a single record per agent that captures onboarding owner, access privileges,

00:04:16.922 --> 00:04:22.822
behavior, and cross-platform capabilities. An over-provisioned email agent with 50 attached tools

00:04:22.822 --> 00:04:24.702
is the example worth investigating.

00:04:26.216 --> 00:04:32.316
Switch from Sandbox AQ now watches AI agents spend, performance metrics and security

00:04:32.316 --> 00:04:35.396
posture in one view, HPC Wire reports.

00:04:36.136 --> 00:04:40.936
Security and finance teams get unified telemetry across every platform an agent runs on.

00:04:41.576 --> 00:04:46.896
Cybersecurity experts told Think Digital Partners that autonomous agents need new digital identity

00:04:46.896 --> 00:04:51.756
frameworks because human-centric controls break down when agents act on their own across

00:04:51.756 --> 00:05:03.872
systems. A builder on Reddit's local Lama forum plans to buy a used HP Z640 with dual E5-2,680v4

00:05:03.872 --> 00:05:14.032
CPUs and 64GB of ECC RAM for 550 euros, then drop in 2 RTX 306012GB cards. The intended mix

00:05:14.032 --> 00:05:21.672
is Q3.8 Flash Next on Strata plus Lama.CPP, PyTorch computer vision training, reinforcement

00:05:21.672 --> 00:05:26.652
learning in Pie Bullet, Laura fine-tuning, and Mini Max H3 video generation.

00:05:27.212 --> 00:05:33.432
Open questions are dual-socket PCIe layout, power limit adapters for the 3060s, whether

00:05:33.432 --> 00:05:40.152
the included Quadro M6000 24GB card still helps under CUDA 12, and chassis thermals that

00:05:40.152 --> 00:05:42.712
hit 86 degrees Celsius during mem test.

00:05:44.569 --> 00:05:49.949
Model Fit is a real-time Mac configurator, posted to that same local Lama community

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:55.069
that shows which large language models fit in memory, and what inference speed to expect

00:05:55.069 --> 00:05:57.149
on every Apple Silicon configuration.

00:05:57.769 --> 00:06:03.129
The estimates come from a model fitted on actual Lama Bench runs, Apple list prices refresh

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:09.249
daily, and the tool is built to help a buyer pick among M4, M5 Pro, and other SKUs for

00:06:09.249 --> 00:06:09.949
local work.

00:06:11.855 --> 00:06:17.215
Low latency streaming speech-to-speech is what voice managerships, over a single web socket,

00:06:17.215 --> 00:06:23.015
with bargin, session memory, and tool-call integration, according to a local Lama post.

00:06:23.515 --> 00:06:27.875
Hermes' console is a Kotlin reference client styled after Star Trek L-Cars.

00:06:28.415 --> 00:06:35.895
The stack uses Nemotron and Breeze TTS-2, and it is out under MIT with client integration docs and a Python client.

00:06:37.054 --> 00:06:46.054
Someone running Gemma 431bq5KM at about 2.3 tokens per second on a single RTX 306012 gigabyte card,

00:06:46.054 --> 00:06:49.894
