00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:40.460
Web pages wrap the useful bits inside navigation.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:47.140
Scripps and ads that agents then strip at token cost, so let me pop the hood on LLMs.TXT.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:50.240
The curated markdown file meant to skip that parse.

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:55.440
The proposal puts one file at the site route that gathers expert level summaries and links

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:59.160
to key pages, and that file is the map and agent reads first.

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:04.800
Context windows are still finite, so every token spent chewing Chrome is a token that never

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:05.660
reaches the answer.

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:11.280
A clean markdown map lets the agent judge relevance before it fetches full pages, which

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:14.200
is the step that used to dump a whole human layout into the prompt.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:19.620
The V2 revision added standard link relations so the agent does not have to guess the URL.

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:25.680
Those relations are real alternate with type text slash markdown, and real describe by.

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:31.540
Open AI and Thropic and Gemini already publish their developer docs this way, and documentation

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:33.940
platforms generate the file automatically.

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:38.440
The engineering trade-off is maintenance overhead versus retrieval quality.

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:43.000
Sites that keep the file current see agents land on the right information faster,

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:46.900
and a stale file is just another outdated asset sitting at the root.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:51.240
Publish one when you already maintain high-quality mark-down documentation

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:55.480
and you want coding agents or retrieval systems to consume it reliably.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:57.920
Skip it when nobody will update the map.

